The Starless Sea, a captivating and mysterious novel by Ruta Sepetys, immerses readers into the world of a young pirate named Faye. Set in 18th-century Europe, Faye is a skilled navigator aboard the Blackbird, a ship captained by her enigmatic uncle, Captain Nightingale. As the story unfolds, Faye discovers a hidden treasure map that promises untold riches and a chance to uncover the truth about her family's past.

Faye's journey takes her on a perilous quest across the treacherous seas, encountering dangerous pirates, mythical sea creatures, and a web of secrets that threaten not only her life but also the fate of her crew. Along the way, she forms unexpected alliances and confronts her own inner demons, learning the value of loyalty, courage, and the power of love.

